      "Language": "fre",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "We report a case of porocephalosis in a 35-year-old Congolese adult who habitually ate large amounts of snake. The principal nonspecific clinical sign was abdominal pain. Diagnosis was based on X-ray examination of the abdomen without preparation and abdominal ultrasound scan."},
